      "Ticketid": "HF-1007",
      "Customername": "Sandra Mills",
      "Subject": "Third delay on my laptop replacement - escalating",
      "Body": "This is the third time my laptop replacement has been pushed. The device shuts down randomly during customer calls. If this isn't resolved this week I'm raising it with the CIO. Ticket references: HW-3321, HW-3398.",
      "Category": "Hardware",
      "Priority": "Medium",
      "Rationale": "The issue is a physical laptop failure/replacement delay, so Hardware fits best. Priority is Medium because one user is degraded during customer calls but the ticket does not state she cannot work at all; KB says High is for cannot work at all. KB supports hardware repair/loaner timing and service desk contact but does not cover repeated replacement delays or a this-week resolution commitment, so the draft escalates without inventing a timeline.",
      "Confidence": 0.86,
      "Draftreply": "soften the tone! Hi Sandra,I\u2019m sorry your laptop replacement has been pushed back again, especially since the device is shutting down randomly during customer calls. I\u2019ve noted the prior references HW-3321 and HW-3398 so the team can review the history together.Based on our hardware support guidance, in-warranty laptop faults should be handled through a Hardware Repair ticket, and loaner devices ship within 2 business days when repairs take longer than 3 days. Because this is the third delay on an active replacement and the timing concern is not covered by the standard guidance, we\u2019re escalating this to a hardware specialist for review rather than giving you an unsupported estimate.If you are unable to work at all, please also call the Service Desk at extension 4357 during staffed hours so the ticket can be handled as High severity.Best regards,HomeFix Supply Support Team"
